back to frame 1. Torso stays near cell center; no whole-body horizontal travel across the cell.\n\nBLADE CONTAINMENT (most important): the curved blade is the only long object. Imagine an invisible safe box covering the central 84% of every cell (8% margin on each side). The ENTIRE blade, from pommel to tip, plus the whole body and cloak, must stay inside that safe box in EVERY frame. During swings bend the elbow and keep the blade close to the body or angled up/down instead of reaching sideways; never let the tip point horizontally toward a neighbouring cell. Nothing from one frame may appear in another cell.\n\nFacing RIGHT in 3/4 view in every frame. Body plus blade only: NO slash arc, NO weapon trail, NO motion lines, NO particles, NO sparks, NO smoke, NO aura, NO afterimages, NO magic circle (effects are separate runtime layers). Keep the blade compact and close to the body so it stays fully inside its own cell; leave a clear magenta margin of at least 5% on all four sides of every cell. Same camera distance and same body scale in all 6 frames; body center stays near the cell center; feet stay on the same ground line except where noted.\nExactly 6 frames in a 3 columns x 2 rows grid of equal square 512x512 cells, total image 1536x1024, read left-to-right then next row. Background 100% solid flat #FF00FF magenta in every cell, no gradient, no floor, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no numbers, no gridlines, no borders, no frames between cells. Clean HD smooth painted, NOT pixel art.\n",
